      "math_academy_id": "q-98163",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,6,\\,-3⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨4,\\,2,\\,10⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[\\frac{2}{3}f(t)+\\frac{1}{2}g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}⟨3,\\,6,\\,-3⟩+\\frac{1}{2}⟨4,\\,2,\\,10⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,\\,4,\\,-2⟩+⟨2,\\,1,\\,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,5,\\,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
